speechtext:
The hon. member for Cardigan (Mr. McQuaid) says, "Far too late".
Clause 30 reads in part:
-under this act, in the same manner and to the same extent as a superior court of record;
Subclause (c) of clause 30 reads:
-whether or not such evidence or information is or would be admissible in a court of law;
This power is far beyond that given to a court. The government is not worried about how it gathers evidence. There has been a great deal of discussion in the last two or three weeks regarding wire tapping, which is not really admissible in a court of law. That would not bother this group. They would use any evidence, no matter how it was obtained or how fair or just it was. They would use it whether or not it would be admissible in 4 court of law.
